WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:02.340
Hello again, dear viewers.

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.750
You know what it is and what it does.

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:09.890
It being The Anom-O-Tron 6000, our hyper-advanced
simulation computer.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:14.630
IT also being one of today’s combatants,
the horrifying creature created by Stephen

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:20.460
King in his 1986 novel - the most popular
form of this shapeshifting, fear-eating monster

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.419
being Pennywise the Dancing Clown.

00:00:23.419 --> 00:00:24.619
And we thought…

00:00:24.619 --> 00:00:31.880
What if Pennywise met the SCP Foundation’s
resident lover of fear, SCP-2006, also known

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.420
as Too Spooky?

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.850
Well, let’s turn on the device and find
out!

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:42.920
It was the summer of 1989, and for all across
the United States, it was the time of freedom,

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:48.149
of childhood wonder, splashing through creeks
searching for frogs, flying kites, and riding

00:00:48.149 --> 00:00:53.649
their bikes as fast and as far as they could
before it was time to be home for dinner.

00:00:53.649 --> 00:00:57.410
At the SCP Foundation, however, there was
no summer break.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:02.579
No lazy days lounging by the pool, no trips
to the corner ice cream shop to sample every

00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:08.370
flavor before finally picking one, and certainly
no trips to the beach.

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:12.940
He never thought he'd say this, but Agent
Adams was beginning to miss dumping sand out

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:18.490
of his shoes at the end of a long day, tending
to the sunburn he always seemed to get.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:23.850
Instead, he was working, sitting on board
a Foundation-owned helicopter, staring down

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:29.360
at the beautiful sun-soaked landscape below
and wishing he too could be having a little

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.460
bit of Summer fun.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:36.440
But there was no time to dwell on the past,
no day for daydreams.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:41.080
He needed to bring his attention back to the
task at hand: transporting this anomaly to

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.230
its new containment site.

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:46.190
It was hard to keep himself focused, he had
to admit.

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:47.700
There wasn't much company on board.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:54.830
It was just him, the pilot, the shy, quiet
Agent Paul, and SCP-2006.

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:58.400
Adams didn't know too much about the entity,
he had to admit.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:03.050
He hadn't seen too much of it, only crossed
paths with it once or twice.

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:07.980
Currently, it was contained in a miniature,
portable version of its airtight containment

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:08.980
cell.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:12.650
The little he had seen of the creature had
been confusing, and, to be honest, a little

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:14.010
bit ridiculous.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:20.700
It was hairy, sort of like a gorilla but more
like a man in a cheap gorilla Halloween costume,

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:25.730
and wore an old-school space helmet on its
head, complete with two goofy antennae jutting

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:26.730
out of the top.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:31.980
He had laughed out loud when he first saw
it, but a supervisor had reprimanded him harshly,

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:36.880
and promised that if he was caught laughing
at SCP-2006 again, he would be reassigned

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:39.120
to a far more dangerous anomaly.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:46.850
He didn't want to screw around with that SCP-682
or SCP-106, so he made sure to stifle his

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:50.420
urge to giggle the next time he saw the absurd
creature.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:54.280
Now, sitting on the helicopter, listening
to the whirring of the blades and wishing

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:58.540
he had thought to bring a book, he couldn't
help but ponder the nature of the entity he

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.430
was helping transport.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:02.390
"So, what's this thing's deal?"

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:06.720
He asked Agent Paul, who had been silently
working on a newspaper crossword puzzle he

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:07.800
brought with him.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.340
"What, SCP-2006?"

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.130
"Yeah, what's up with it?

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.020
It's kind of...silly, right?"

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.880
Agent Paul's eyes widened, and he put a finger
to his lips.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:16.880
"Shh!

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:18.220
You can't say stuff like that."

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:20.390
Agent Adams held up his hands in surprise.

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:22.400
"Whoa, buddy, sorry to offend."

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:23.630
"No, no."

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:24.950
Agent Paul shook his head.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.160
"You don't get it.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.390
We need to act like this thing is terrifying.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:29.390
Got it?"

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:30.390
He lowered his voice.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:33.500
"I know it's kind of funny, when I first saw
the thing it transformed into a killer tomato

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:37.100
from an old movie for crying out loud, but
the higher-ups don't want it to figure out

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.350
what actually scares people.

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.099
So we have to play along.

00:03:41.099 --> 00:03:44.430
Like when a little kid jumps out from behind
a chair in a monster mask and you give them

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:46.660
a big fake scream so they can feel powerful.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.040
It's like that.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.599
Only the fate of humanity rests in the balance."

00:03:50.599 --> 00:03:54.940
Agent Adams couldn't help himself at that
comment.

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:55.940
"Seriously?

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:58.950
How does protecting this thing's ego affect
the fate of humanity?"

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:02.770
Agent Paul rolled his eyes so hard it looked
like he might hurt himself.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:04.920
"Because, Adams.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:10.120
This is a creature whose only goal in the
world, its favorite thing to do, its entire

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:13.370
life's purpose, is to scare human beings.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:14.370
That's all it wants.

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:17.909
Right now, it's not that great at it because
its idea of what's scary is based on a bunch

00:04:17.909 --> 00:04:22.420
of horrible drive-in horror movies from the
50s, but if it ever figured out the kind of

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:24.080
stuff that really scares people?

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:27.759
I mean really, truly, pee your pants level
scares people?

00:04:27.759 --> 00:04:29.409
Who knows what it would do?

00:04:29.409 --> 00:04:32.169
Imagine if, say, this thing got a look at
SCP-173.

00:04:32.169 --> 00:04:35.960
Or even a more recent horror movie, like what
if this thing saw A Nightmare on Elm Street

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:39.370
and decided to start cutting people up with
Freddy Kreuger hands?

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:42.300
Seriously, you need to learn to think before
you speak."

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:46.740
Agent Adams nodded thoughtfully, taking in
the surprising outburst from such a usually

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:47.740
quiet guy.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:50.120
"Well okay, dang, I had no idea."

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:53.370
"Maybe you should pay more attention during
briefings."

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:54.860
Agent Paul snarked.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:59.729
Adams was just about to retort, when the helicopter
suddenly veered to the left with a lurch.

00:04:59.729 --> 00:05:04.069
There was a grinding sound, metal on metal,
and it quickly became apparent that something

00:05:04.069 --> 00:05:05.440
was wrong with the helicopter.

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:08.660
"Something's wrong, I've never seen anything
like this before!"

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.690
The pilot shouted from his position at the
controls.

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:14.069
"This thing's going down, and we're going
to have to jump if we don't want to go down

00:05:14.069 --> 00:05:15.069
with it!"

00:05:15.069 --> 00:05:16.979
"What about SCP-2006?"

00:05:16.979 --> 00:05:17.979
Agent Paul panicked.

00:05:17.979 --> 00:05:21.270
"Unless it has a parachute, we'll have to
leave it to fend for itself!"

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:25.009
The pilot was already suiting up with his
own emergency parachute, making his way to

00:05:25.009 --> 00:05:26.099
the door of the helicopter.

00:05:26.099 --> 00:05:29.809
"I suggest you get moving if you don't feel
like exploding today!"

00:05:29.809 --> 00:05:35.069
That was all Agent Adams needed to shock him
out of his temporary crisis-induced paralysis.

00:05:35.069 --> 00:05:40.380
He grabbed the last two parachutes on board,
tossed one to the pale, extremely sweaty Agent

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:44.240
Paul, and prepared to make the jump to what
would hopefully be safety.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:48.779
He patted the side of SCP-2006's mobile containment
unit halfheartedly.

00:05:48.779 --> 00:05:49.990
"Sorry, buddy."

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:54.229
was all he could think to say before he took
a deep breath, tried not to throw up, and

00:05:54.229 --> 00:05:57.689
followed the pilot, diving out of the helicopter
toward the ground below.

00:05:57.689 --> 00:06:01.629
He heard Agent Paul jump out right behind
him, and soon the only sound he could hear

00:06:01.629 --> 00:06:06.129
was the roaring of the wind in his ears as
his fingers fumbled with the ripcord on his

00:06:06.129 --> 00:06:07.129
harness.

00:06:07.129 --> 00:06:10.919
He pulled it, and the parachute ballooned
out, doing its job and carrying him slowly

00:06:10.919 --> 00:06:12.319
down to earth.

00:06:12.319 --> 00:06:15.550
He landed with a grunt, feeling around for
any broken bones.

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:17.310
Thankfully, he had landed smoothly.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:22.070
A few moments later, Agent Paul landed a great
deal less smoothly, but still very much in

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:23.129
one piece.

00:06:23.129 --> 00:06:26.629
The pilot was already dusting himself off
several feet away from the two men.

00:06:26.629 --> 00:06:30.599
In the distance, they could hear the booming
sound of the helicopter crashing, and Agent

00:06:30.599 --> 00:06:31.869
Adams winced.

00:06:31.869 --> 00:06:33.150
"Poor guy."

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:34.439
"Poor us."

00:06:34.439 --> 00:06:35.460
Agent Paul added.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:36.710
"Where are we, anyway?"

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:37.840
"Somewhere in Maine."

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:38.840
The pilot shrugged.

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:40.659
"Small town nearby, from the looks of it."

00:06:40.659 --> 00:06:44.860
He pointed toward a nearby sign, and the other
two men sighed with relief.

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:45.930
Civilization.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:50.400
Somewhere they could get cleaned up, get a
bite to eat, and apologetically call for backup.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:51.400
"Nice."

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:52.400
Agent Adams grinned.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.699
"Paul, you're from this part of the country,
you know this town?

00:06:54.699 --> 00:06:55.699
Derry?"

00:06:55.699 --> 00:06:56.949
Agent Paul shook his head.

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:58.710
"No, I've never even heard of it."

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:02.879
Agent Adams shrugged, and he, Agent Paul,
and the pilot slowly made their way into the

00:07:02.879 --> 00:07:05.560
unassuming little town of Derry, Maine.

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:10.499
It was lovely, idyllic even, such a picture
of small-town bliss that they didn't even

00:07:10.499 --> 00:07:15.389
notice just how many "Missing" posters were
stapled to the telephone poles, the wide eyes

00:07:15.389 --> 00:07:18.690
of lost children seeming to watch them as
they passed.

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:22.779
Meanwhile, on the other side of town, in the
middle of the marshy barrens where so many

00:07:22.779 --> 00:07:28.119
children had gone missing that summer, and
the summer 27 years before it, a figure was

00:07:28.119 --> 00:07:31.449
climbing out of the smoldering wreckage of
the helicopter.

00:07:31.449 --> 00:07:38.030
It was big, and furry, with massive paws and
that silly metal helmet on top of its head.

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:43.729
SCP-2006 had survived and was taking its first
free steps in decades.

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:49.069
It looked around at the wilderness, the trees,
the rocks, the running water, and the entrance

00:07:49.069 --> 00:07:50.819
to the town's sewers.

00:07:50.819 --> 00:07:56.419
It barely understood any of what it was seeing,
but it knew that it was in a brand new place,

00:07:56.419 --> 00:07:59.610
one that would hopefully be filled with brand
new people to scare.

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:06.180
Oh, how exciting to think about seeing new
faces, eyes wide with dread, mouths open in

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:07.180
screams!

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:09.819
The creature was in its favorite, most fearsome
form, too!

00:08:09.819 --> 00:08:14.830
The mighty and terrible Ro-Man from the 1953
classic "Robot Monster."

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:18.969
None could behold this shape without collapsing
in terror.

00:08:18.969 --> 00:08:23.379
SCP-2006 clapped its hands together delightedly,
laughing to itself.

00:08:23.379 --> 00:08:26.869
It had been nervous, when the helicopter started
to fall out of the sky.

00:08:26.869 --> 00:08:27.869
But now?

00:08:27.869 --> 00:08:31.159
It seemed like that was the best thing that
could have possibly happened!

00:08:31.159 --> 00:08:36.669
With no one in the immediate vicinity to frighten,
2006 decided to wander off through the woods

00:08:36.669 --> 00:08:39.050
in search of fresh victims.

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:44.420
After all, now that it was free from that
awful box, there was plenty of time to look,

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:47.210
and an endless amount of scares to be given!

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:51.740
The creature ambled down the road, past a
public park, a vintage diner, and rows and

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:53.490
rows of little houses.

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:55.500
A woman passed, walking her dog.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:09:00.990
SCP-2006 roared at her, expanding its arms
wide and standing up on its tiptoe to appear

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:02.399
as large as possible.

00:09:02.399 --> 00:09:03.540
"FEAR ME!

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:05.339
FOR I AM RO-MAN!"

00:09:05.339 --> 00:09:07.490
"That's nice, dear."

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:11.220
The lady passively remarked, stopping to let
her dog sniff 2006's leg.

00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:14.740
It lifted its own leg, and urinated on the
creature's fur.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.399
"How DARE YOU!

00:09:16.399 --> 00:09:18.050
I am MONSTROUS!

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:19.709
Quake with fear!"

00:09:19.709 --> 00:09:24.880
2006 bellowed, but the lady only chuckled,
shook her head, and continued on her way.

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:29.720
Puzzled, the creature continued to walk along
the road, looking for more victims to terrorize

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:32.120
and strike fear into their fragile hearts.

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:35.600
Up ahead, a group of little children playing
with a soccer ball.

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:36.600
Perfect.

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:41.600
2006 crouched low to the ground, and snuck
up on the group, hiding behind a bush before

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:43.170
popping out with a wild yell.

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:46.060
"TREMBLE BEFORE THE MIGHTY RO-MAN!"

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:47.100
It shouted.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:50.959
One child screamed, startled, but his friends
immediately began to tease him.

00:09:50.959 --> 00:09:53.959
"Calm down ya big baby, it's just a guy in
a suit."

00:09:53.959 --> 00:09:56.130
One of his friends thumped him with the soccer
ball.

00:09:56.130 --> 00:10:00.279
Another boy, who was eating a cherry popsicle,
laughed loudly at the sight of the entity.

00:10:00.279 --> 00:10:01.740
"Nice costume, loser."

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:07.260
He blew a raspberry, and threw the popsicle
at 2006's head, sugary frozen slurry dripping

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:08.509
down its fur.

00:10:08.509 --> 00:10:10.990
"Why aren't you afraid?"

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:16.130
SCP-2006 demanded, unable to grasp how it
had lost its scaring abilities so quickly.

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:20.010
Perhaps something had gone wrong during the
crash, or perhaps this town was just filled

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:22.370
with unusually brave people.

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:26.600
Whatever it was, 2006 wanted to figure out
the answer, and fast.

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:30.570
After all, who was SCP-2006 if it wasn't scary?

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:34.630
"Because we're not scared of some nerd in
a Chewbacca suit, barf bag!"

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:38.870
The kid with the soccer ball threw it at 2006,
who caught it, its claws puncturing the ball

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:39.870
and flattening it.

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:41.350
"Hey, this doofus broke our ball!

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:42.350
Kick his butt!"

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:45.620
"It is you who should be concerned with your
butts!"

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:50.800
SCP-2006 retorted, changing its face to the
shape of a werewolf from a classic black and

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:52.009
white film.

00:10:52.009 --> 00:10:57.000
It bared its teeth, rubbery tongue lolling
out of its mouth, glassy eyes staring in two

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.000
different directions.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.160
"Woah, how'd you do that?"

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:02.730
The angry boy lowered his fists, gaping in
awe.

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:04.529
"Never mind, that was kind of cool."

00:11:04.529 --> 00:11:06.399
"Bummer about the ball though."

00:11:06.399 --> 00:11:07.759
The first boy sighed.

00:11:07.759 --> 00:11:13.421
Fed up with all of this confusion, SCP-2006
dropped the deflated ball to the ground, then

00:11:13.421 --> 00:11:16.290
promptly turned and walked in the opposite
direction.

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:18.139
"Hey, where's he going?!"

00:11:18.139 --> 00:11:20.839
The kids demanded, but the anomaly did not
respond.

00:11:20.839 --> 00:11:24.800
One boy began bragging about his new collection
of baseball cards, and their attention was

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:29.339
soon pulled away from the strange being that
they believed to be a person in a monster

00:11:29.339 --> 00:11:30.339
costume.

00:11:30.339 --> 00:11:36.629
Then, as SCP-2006 walked, it heard the sound
it had been waiting to hear all day.

00:11:36.629 --> 00:11:42.810
Screams, glorious screams of absolute terror,
the purest sound of fear.

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:46.730
It sounded like a child, shrieking at the
top of their lungs in the face of something

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:48.589
truly horrifying.

00:11:48.589 --> 00:11:50.879
Where could that wonderful noise be coming
from?

00:11:50.879 --> 00:11:55.500
And why hadn't SCP-2006 been the one to inspire
it?!

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:58.180
The anomaly was desperate to get to the bottom
of things.

00:11:58.180 --> 00:12:03.459
It followed the sound, searching for its source,
but just as the sound grew louder and the

00:12:03.459 --> 00:12:07.839
creature got closer, it cut off all of a sudden,
as if swallowed up by something all-encompassing.

00:12:07.839 --> 00:12:08.839
"Hello?!"

00:12:08.839 --> 00:12:10.879
SCP-2006 called out, in vain.

00:12:10.879 --> 00:12:12.920
"Where did you go?

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:15.620
Come back, so that I can scare you!

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:16.620
Please!

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:17.620
...I am Ro-Man!"

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:18.620
"Hiya there, Ro-Man!"

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:22.090
A voice piped up from behind the entity.

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:24.790
It spun around, looking for whoever just spoke.

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:25.790
"Hello?

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:27.190
Who is it?"

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:33.170
SCP-2006 could not see anyone, only the suburban
street, the houses, the empty yards.

00:12:33.170 --> 00:12:34.410
"Down here!"

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:35.440
The voice called.

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:36.509
"This way!"

00:12:36.509 --> 00:12:40.139
The voice was coming from a storm drain, down
in the darkness below.

00:12:40.139 --> 00:12:45.980
SCP-2006 could just barely make out a pair
of eyes, a white painted face, a red nose,

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:48.550
and a pair of bright red lips.

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:49.550
"BOO!"

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:52.420
SCP-2006 shouted at the person in the storm
drain.

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:54.939
It burst into a fit of giggles.

00:12:54.939 --> 00:12:57.959
"Oh, that was very good.

00:12:57.959 --> 00:12:58.959
What's your name?"

00:12:58.959 --> 00:12:59.959
The clown asked.

00:12:59.959 --> 00:13:02.459
"I am Ro-Man, the mighty, the fearsome!"

00:13:02.459 --> 00:13:03.459
SCP-2006 replied.

00:13:03.459 --> 00:13:05.790
"Nice to meet ya.

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:09.569
I'm Pennywise, the dancing clown!"

00:13:09.569 --> 00:13:12.399
The clown grinned, showing a mouth full of
sharp teeth.

00:13:12.399 --> 00:13:14.990
"Come a little closer, why don't ya.

00:13:14.990 --> 00:13:17.980
Maybe we could be friends."

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:20.930
SCP-2006 was perplexed, but approached just
the same.

00:13:20.930 --> 00:13:26.500
The clown took a deep breath, catching a whiff
of the entity's unfamiliar scent, and it frowned.

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:28.000
"What are you?"

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:31.850
Pennywise asked, the friendly affectation
gone from its voice and face.

00:13:31.850 --> 00:13:36.860
"You don't smell right to me...not like anything
I've ever smelled."

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:38.050
"I told you.

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:39.589
Are you scared?"

00:13:39.589 --> 00:13:41.050
2006 replied.

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:44.680
Pennywise laughed at this, a wild unhinged
cackle.

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:48.959
"I'm not scared of you.

00:13:48.959 --> 00:13:50.459
Are you scared?"

00:13:50.459 --> 00:13:55.060
The clown stared at 2006, its wide orange
eyes glinting in the light.

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:56.110
"Of course not.

00:13:56.110 --> 00:13:58.980
I'm much scarier than you are."

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:01.500
"You're funny!"

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:03.699
The clown exclaimed.

00:14:03.699 --> 00:14:05.110
"Very funny.

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:07.730
Why don't you come down here with me?

00:14:07.730 --> 00:14:08.790
Want to float?

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:11.300
We all do, down here."

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:13.399
"I'm not funny."

00:14:13.399 --> 00:14:14.800
SCP-2006 pouted.

00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:16.199
"I'm scary."

00:14:16.199 --> 00:14:19.430
"Sure, sure, whatever you say."

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:21.019
The clown waved the words away.

00:14:21.019 --> 00:14:23.249
"Don't you want to come over here?

00:14:23.249 --> 00:14:24.649
We could be friends."

00:14:24.649 --> 00:14:29.060
Cautiously, the anomaly approached the storm
drain, leaning down to get a better look at

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:30.470
the strange clown.

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:35.149
Suddenly, the clown's hand shot out, grabbing
hold of SCP-2006's arm.

00:14:35.149 --> 00:14:40.639
The clown's mouth stretched open wide, revealing
row upon row of teeth, and a seemingly impossible

00:14:40.639 --> 00:14:43.589
stretch of darkness inside of its jaws.

00:14:43.589 --> 00:14:48.389
Pennywise bit down on the anomaly's arm, pulling
it into the storm drain, trying to swallow

00:14:48.389 --> 00:14:51.110
it whole like a snake swallows its prey.

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:57.440
But as it tried to devour SCP-2006, it began
to choke, its body rejecting the entity, and

00:14:57.440 --> 00:15:00.459
it spat the furry anomaly back out.

00:15:00.459 --> 00:15:05.380
SCP-2006 landed in the water inside of the
sewer with a wet plop, as Pennywise rubbed

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:07.649
at its jaw thoughtfully.

00:15:07.649 --> 00:15:08.649
"Hm.

00:15:08.649 --> 00:15:10.899
You really are strange."

00:15:10.899 --> 00:15:11.899
The clown frowned.

00:15:11.899 --> 00:15:15.360
"I told you before, I'm scary.

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:16.970
I'm scary!"

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:18.589
SCP-2006 insisted.

00:15:18.589 --> 00:15:20.129
"Sure you are."

00:15:20.129 --> 00:15:21.129
Pennywise grimaced.

00:15:21.129 --> 00:15:23.199
"Is that the shape you use?

00:15:23.199 --> 00:15:24.420
To scare people?"

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:25.839
SCP-2006 nodded.

00:15:25.839 --> 00:15:27.260
"Among others.

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:29.449
This is my most successful, though."

00:15:29.449 --> 00:15:30.870
Pennywise shook its head.

00:15:30.870 --> 00:15:37.240
"I know a thing or two about fear, it's what
I use to season my meat.

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:39.620
Fear is what I do.

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:40.699
And you?

00:15:40.699 --> 00:15:43.160
You've got a lot to learn about fear."

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:44.930
"Would you...show me?

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:48.230
How to be more scary?"

00:15:48.230 --> 00:15:49.930
SCP-2006 asked.

00:15:49.930 --> 00:15:55.069
Pennywise laughed again, a hacking, coughing
sound.

00:15:55.069 --> 00:15:57.009
"You know what?

00:15:57.009 --> 00:15:58.490
I will.

00:15:58.490 --> 00:16:01.639
The more frightened children in this town,
the better.

00:16:01.639 --> 00:16:05.610
As long as you understand, this is my turf."

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:07.649
SCP-2006 nodded furiously.

00:16:07.649 --> 00:16:09.019
"I understand!"

00:16:09.019 --> 00:16:14.070
Pennywise beckoned the entity over, and motioned
for it to sit down.

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:15.480
"Fear is...personal.

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:20.279
Everyone is afraid of something different,
and there is a unique way to tap into each

00:16:20.279 --> 00:16:22.290
person's deepest fears.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:24.519
Normally, I look like this.

00:16:24.519 --> 00:16:27.139
Like Pennywise, the Dancing Clown.

00:16:27.139 --> 00:16:32.819
Clowns are funny, children like clowns, but
they're also...terrified of clowns."

00:16:32.819 --> 00:16:35.420
Pennywise did a little jig, laughing wildly.

00:16:35.420 --> 00:16:41.900
"It makes them taste so sweet, when they meet
me like this and think I'm a friend, and then...I

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:43.870
show them what I truly am."

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:45.519
The clown bared its teeth.

00:16:45.519 --> 00:16:47.480
"Humans aren't scared of clowns."

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:49.160
SCP-2006 shook its head.

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:52.290
"In my experience, they only think clowns
are funny.

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:53.290
They laugh at them.

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:55.190
Now this is scary..."

00:16:55.190 --> 00:16:59.009
SCP-2006 concentrated, and changed its shape.

00:16:59.009 --> 00:17:02.439
It was a giant rabbit, from the film Night
of the Lepus.

00:17:02.439 --> 00:17:04.620
"This strikes terror into their hearts."

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:06.550
"No, it doesn't."

00:17:06.550 --> 00:17:08.200
Pennywise rolled its eyes.

00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:09.470
"Listen to me.

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:12.520
Suppose, a child has a fear of birds.

00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:18.860
Maybe he watched a movie about a giant pterodactyl,
maybe he was attacked by a bird as a baby.

00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:19.970
Maybe it was both.

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:22.400
You could try something like this."

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:27.790
Pennywise shifted forms then, changing from
a clown to a giant bird, with sharp talons,

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:31.390
a massive wingspan, a pointed beak, and wild
eyes.

00:17:31.390 --> 00:17:36.980
"Or say the child is afraid to cross a stream,
because he's afraid of piranhas..."

00:17:36.980 --> 00:17:42.240
The shape of Pennywise changed again, as piranhas
plopped into the water below, swimming around

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:44.180
in a ravenous swarm.

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:47.000
"So...being scary is about animals?"

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:50.730
SCP-2006 cocked its head to the side, confused.

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:54.930
Pennywise resumed its clown form, growing
increasingly frustrated.

00:17:54.930 --> 00:18:02.470
"No, it's...it's about a person's darkest
thoughts, the images that come to them while

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:06.230
they lie in bed and struggle to fall asleep.

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:11.550
Say...there's a little boy who lives in fear
of sickness.

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:14.840
His mother planted the fear in his head, you
see.

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:20.050
All day long, he imagines little bacteria
crawling across his skin, infections waiting

00:18:20.050 --> 00:18:23.390
to slip inside and rot him from the inside
out.

00:18:23.390 --> 00:18:26.020
To him, I would look like this..."

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:30.900
Pennywise changed into the shape of a leper,
a man covered with sores and limbs about to

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:33.840
drop off, with a hacking, diseased cough.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:36.710
Then, whoosh, it was a clown again.

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:44.770
"Or say there's a girl who fears one person
more than anyone else in the world: her father.

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:50.780
A man who was once kind to her, maybe, but
loss, anger, and drink have turned him wrong.

00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:54.120
Made anger curdle into violence inside his
heart.

00:18:54.120 --> 00:19:01.720
To her, I would only need to look like him,
to say all of the things she's afraid he thinks..."

00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:03.390
Pennywise looked at SCP-2006.

00:19:03.390 --> 00:19:06.040
"Do you understand now?"

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:07.330
"I think so!"

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:08.330
The anomaly chirped.

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.680
"So I should try something like this!"

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:14.320
It transformed into something large, smooth,
and slimy.

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:17.750
It was one of the frogs from the 1972 film,
"Frogs."

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:21.420
"This will bring any person to their knees
with fright!"

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:22.420
"NO!"

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:23.420
Pennywise bellowed.

00:19:23.420 --> 00:19:25.320
"No, no, no, no, no!

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:26.880
You don't get it!

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:31.230
So many things are scary, spiders, being abandoned
by your friends, being unloved, being buried

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:34.660
alive, a man with no head, a missing poster
for someone who isn't missing yet.

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:35.660
But you?

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:39.820
You're not scary, you're not scary at all!"

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:40.820
SCP-2006 huffed.

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:41.840
"Even when I do this?"

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:46.970
It turned into the shape of a fluffy alien
with glowing red eyes and decidedly fake-looking

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:48.710
papier mache arms.

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:53.180
Pennywise the Dancing Clown sat down on the
ground, resting his head in his hands with

00:19:53.180 --> 00:19:55.560
a long, exhausted sigh.

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:57.180
"Listen, kid.

00:19:57.180 --> 00:20:02.180
I thought this would be fun, but...I'm just
so tired.

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:03.740
You're not scary.

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:05.640
I can't eat you.

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:07.820
What am I supposed to do with you?

00:20:07.820 --> 00:20:14.410
I've got a good thing going here, and I have
for a very, very long time.

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:15.910
You being here?

00:20:15.910 --> 00:20:18.020
It's messing things up.

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:21.650
Just...Get out of my town, you're embarrassing
me.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:23.440
Go on, get out of Derry.

00:20:23.440 --> 00:20:25.590
Find some other town to "scare," this one's
full."

00:20:25.590 --> 00:20:26.590
b

00:20:26.590 --> 00:20:28.490
"Well, you didn't have to be so rude about
it."

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:31.880
SCP-2006 huffed, but it listened just the
same.

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:37.120
It left Derry, Maine behind, walking off down
the open road, just in time for an unmarked

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:42.010
van from the SCP Foundation to pull up beside
it, and open the door.

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:43.120
"Ro-Man!"

00:20:43.120 --> 00:20:44.120
Called out Agent Paul.

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:48.240
"You're very frightening, and we almost didn't
stop because you frightened us so much, but...do

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:49.560
you need a ride?

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:52.720
In exchange for promising not to tear us apart
with your mighty claws, of course."

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:56.000
"Will you take me to more people I can scare?"

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:57.000
2006 asked.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:00.520
Agent Paul hid his smile, and beckoned the
creature inside.

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:02.660
"You got it, buddy."

00:21:02.660 --> 00:21:08.640
Now go check out “SCP-2006 - Too Spooky”
and “25 Most Frightening SCP” for more

00:21:08.640 --> 00:21:12.390
terrifying journeys into the world of the
SCP Foundation!

